Package: lucid-everything-icon-theme
Source: lucidos-icon-themes
Version: 0.3.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Javid Medina <javidamedina@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: 51576
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Description: broad icon coverage beneath the LucidOS themes (GPL-3.0)
 Lucid-Everything, a renamed copy of WhiteSur-icon-theme by vinceliuice. It
 covers the third-party applications that LucidOS does not draw icons for, and
 sits one link down the fallback chain from Lucid and Lucid-Dark:
 .
     Lucid  ->  Lucid-Everything  ->  hicolor
 .
 It is a separate package because it is under a separate licence. This is
 somebody else's work under the GPL-3.0, and the GPL does not permit adding
 restrictions to what it covers -- so it cannot be shipped inside a package
 whose licence is NonCommercial. Splitting the tree along the licence boundary
 makes that a fact dpkg enforces rather than a paragraph in a file.
 .
 Attribution and the list of changes are in
 /usr/share/icons/Lucid-Everything/AUTHORS; the licence text is beside it in
 COPYING.
